00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:40.800
On a sunny day, a queen honeybee leaves her hive.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.920
Male bees, called drones, follow her.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.720
The queen mates with a drone.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.450
Now she can lay eggs.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.400
The queen flies back to the hive.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.740
Laying many eggs is her job.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.500
Puts one egg in each cell.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.170
Three days, the eggs hatch.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.240
Out come larvae.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.220
Worker bees feed the larvae.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.660
After five or six days, workers cover the larvae cells.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.560
Inside the cell, the larva grows into a pupa.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.980
In about ten days, a young...

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:40.490
out of the cell. Hives have only one queen. Most other bees are workers. Some bees are drones.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:49.820
Workers are females. Drones are males. Young worker bees stay inside the hive. They clean

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:59.970
cells and make food. Workers make wax to build cells. Some cells are for eggs.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:11.580
other cells are for food sometimes the hive is too hot the wax begins to melt

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:17.640
