00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:07.250
alone. We'll get you and your friends laughing out loud. Do you read this book? And I'm sure

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:12.870
you'll like it. Share it with your family. It'll make for some great laughs. Try to get

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.190
your hands on Going Buggy.

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:35.500
Hey Emmett, how are you doing?

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:36.780
Good Tony, how are you doing?

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:37.440
Good.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:38.500
Got a package there for you.

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:39.040
Well thanks.

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:40.320
Okay, you be careful now.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:40.900
I will.

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:41.620
See you later.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:42.920
What you got here, Tony?

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:43.720
A package.

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:45.150
Whoa!

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:46.070
Bees!

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:47.180
In the mail?

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:47.840
Sure.

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:49.640
Let's go get suited up and start a new hive.

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:50.200
Alright.

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:57.570
Now why is it that they're all crowded around the top and around the can in the center there?

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.960
Well they've clustered on the can of sugar...

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.780
which is what feeds them on their way up from the south.

00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:06.840
And you'll notice it's screened so they don't suffocate while they're in the trucks.

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:08.210
Where did these bees come from?

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:09.410
They came from Georgia.

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:10.570
Well, they must be tired.

00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:11.450
I guess.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:15.050
So what's the first thing that we have to do in order to start the new hive?

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:18.550
Well, the first thing, we should feed them with a little sugar syrup.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:23.030
And if you'd paint the screens, they'll start making wax on the foundation we're going to give them.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.200
They're drinking it right away. They love this.

00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:33.910
What's in this? Sugar and water?

00:22:34.090 --> 00:22:35.650
Sugar and water.

00:22:38.060 --> 00:22:40.800
Now why do we want to feed them before we put them in their new home?

00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:43.640
Well, we want them to stay once we shake them in there.

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:46.900
So if they have a nice full stomach, they can immediately start making wax.

00:22:47.100 --> 00:22:50.350
Ah, and they'll make this new hive their own, huh?

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:50.770
That's right.

00:22:54.730 --> 00:22:55.850
Just paint it on here, huh?

00:22:56.980 --> 00:22:57.560
You're doing great.

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:11.240
Now the next step is to pry off the lid, and you'll notice the can's right there so the bees don't...

00:23:11.780 --> 00:23:13.340
Right, the bees don't just fly out.

00:23:13.420 --> 00:23:17.030
That's right. And you see this string here? That's what the queen cage is attached to.

00:23:17.130 --> 00:23:20.350
So while the bees are traveling, the queen is actually kept separate from the rest of the hive.

00:23:20.390 --> 00:23:20.790
That's right.

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:21.740
And now?

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:26.900
Well, before we pull the can, we've got to give the bees a jar so they all fall to the bottom of the cage.

00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:39.360
And I'll kind of shake that can so we don't get any bees.

00:23:39.660 --> 00:23:42.850
And you see here's where they feed.

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:45.550
They just stick their little tongues in there and drink, huh?

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:46.590
That's right, right through the gauze.

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:48.560
And I'll pull the queen out.

00:23:49.550 --> 00:23:50.750
And you can see there's the queen.

00:23:50.850 --> 00:23:51.510
There she is.

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:55.170
And she's got her attendants in there too, huh?

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:55.870
That's right.

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:58.560
Then let's put the bees in their new home.

00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:26.140
Now we're ready to put the queen in.

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:28.860
But before we do, we'll pull the cork out of one end.

00:24:29.280 --> 00:24:29.980
You'll notice the camera.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:30.360
Here

00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:32.900
So the bees will eat through the candy.

00:24:33.290 --> 00:24:34.890
And then the queen will be able to get out.

00:24:36.070 --> 00:24:37.230
Okay, here you go

00:24:37.930 --> 00:24:39.230
and if you would be kind enough to

00:24:39.690 --> 00:24:41.190
Put the rest of the frames in the hive.

00:24:41.780 --> 00:24:42.780
This is how I can go to work.

00:24:44.940 --> 00:24:45.740
Slide them in, huh?

00:24:46.380 --> 00:24:47.020
All the way over.

00:24:52.140 --> 00:24:52.380
Like that.

00:24:53.160 --> 00:24:54.280
Now we're ready to close her up.

00:24:58.380 --> 00:24:59.080
First, the inner cover.

00:25:01.240 --> 00:25:02.120
and the outer cover.

00:25:03.380 --> 00:25:04.000
And that's that.

00:25:04.410 --> 00:25:06.570
Well, now, how long will it take before they're making honey, Tony?

00:25:06.970 --> 00:25:08.510
Within a couple days, they'll be making honey.

00:25:08.980 --> 00:25:13.100
Unbelievable. I had no idea that bees were such fascinating creatures.

00:25:25.400 --> 00:25:27.840
I know why bees are so busy.

00:25:28.500 --> 00:25:29.940
They make enough honey to feed themselves.

00:25:30.420 --> 00:25:32.560
and to give us a sweet treat, too.

00:25:33.320 --> 00:25:34.160
But most important,

00:25:34.570 --> 00:25:36.410
by buzzing from flower to flower,

00:25:36.900 --> 00:25:37.980
Bees spread pollen.

00:25:38.600 --> 00:25:41.740
pollen to help grow flowers and vegetables and fruit.

00:25:42.380 --> 00:25:43.040
Like this apple.

00:25:44.040 --> 00:25:45.220
So thanks, bees, and...

00:25:45.450 --> 00:25:46.490
And keep up the good work.

00:25:48.840 --> 00:25:51.700
I'll be seeing you next time.

00:25:52.780 --> 00:25:52.960
You

